    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on the Owner read model, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec), documenting the fixed table.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 \n   - Added the `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(timezone(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - Added the fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`).\n   - Added a `timezone(Owner)` method that looks up `REGION_TIMEZONE.get(locality(owner))`, reusing the existing `locality`/region derivation so timezone stays in lock-step with locality. It returns `null` (field omitted) when the owner is absent or the region has no known timezone (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` passes (an owner in Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`), and all 263 tests remain green.",
